    "q-61874": {
      "dom_id": "step-q61874",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "A car is purchased for  $\\$18\\,000$ and its value depreciates (decreases) by $\\frac{1}{5}$ per year. What will be the value of the car in $8$ years?",
      "worked_solution": "If the value reduces by $\\frac{1}{5},$ it means that $\\frac{4}{5}$ of its value remains every year.\n\nTherefore:\n\n- After $1$ year, the value of the car will be $\\$18\\,000\\cdot (\\frac{4}{5}).$\n\n- After $2$ years, the value of the car will be $\\$18\\,000\\cdot {(\\frac{4}{5})}^{2}.$\n\n- After $3$ years, the value of the car will be $\\$18\\,000\\cdot {(\\frac{4}{5})}^{3}.$\n\n- $…$\n\nRepeating this pattern, we see that the value of the car will be $\\$18\\,000\\cdot {(\\frac{4}{5})}^{8}$ in $8$ years.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
