    "q-61968": {
      "dom_id": "step-q61968",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Initially, a company had $1\\,200$ subscribers for its online video channel. The number of subscribers then decreased at a rate of $4%$ every year. Approximately how many subscribers remained after $7$ years?",
      "worked_solution": "The number $4%$ (expressed as a decimal) is equal to $0.04.$ Therefore, a decrease of $4%$ corresponds to multiplication by a factor of:\n\n$$\n1-0.04=0.96\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- After $1$ year, there were $1\\,200\\cdot (0.96)$ subscribers.\n\n- After $2$ years, there were approximately $1\\,200\\cdot (0.96)^{2}$ subscribers.\n\n- After $3$ years, there were approximately $1\\,200\\cdot (0.96)^{3}$ subscribers.\n\n- $…$\n\nRepeating this pattern, we see that there were approximately $1\\,200\\cdot (0.96)^{7}$ subscribers after $7$ years.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-61968-a",
